{"id":"by-3xpq","title":"Beryl 3D build directories grow to 40-50 GB each with stale artifacts","description":"Symptom: free disk fell from 306 GB (2026-11-14) to 162 GB (00:10 UTC 2026-11-16) to 132 GB (02:10 UTC). $BERYL_CACHE/b3d/target is 44 GB, and rust/beryl3d/target in slot-01, -03, -04, -06 and -08 is 46-53 GB each (du, which counts APFS clones at full size, so shared blocks are counted more than once). The b3d sweep's four work trees hold 37-49 GB each. The main workspace's targets are 8-14 GB.

Cause: $BERYL_CACHE/b3d/target/debug/deps holds 77,077 files, with 5,000-6,000 files each for beryl_session, beryl_search and beryl_scene (nine copies of libberyl_scene-*.rlib at 122-157 MB). `sweep.save_target` (tools/src/beryl_tools/beryl3d/sweep.py) removes incremental folders but never removes artifacts that the current build no longer uses, so every saved cache carries all earlier builds, and every worktree clones it in `cli.warm_target`. The main workspace's cache is pruned by `warm.prune` (BUDGET_GB = 15); the Beryl 3D one is not.

Proposed: prune deps/ and build/ to the artifacts the last build used (for example by the newest fingerprint per unit, or by atime/mtime since the build began) before saving, and apply the same budget eviction to worktree and sweep work-tree targets. Done when the saved cache is under 15 GB and free disk stops falling day over day.","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-16T02:39:36Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-16T02:39:36Z","labels":["ci-structure","tier:opus"]}

