{"id":"by-a8g","title":"Long-think search wins sooner and loses later","description":"Derek's playtesting: the deep agents play randomly when far ahead or far behind. In run-003, 45% of pimc18/omniscient/rollout/tuned@10M's searched decisions (1,866 of 4,118) are in positions it rates above 0.95 or below 0.05, and in 89% of those the runner-up is within 0.01 of the best: every move wins (or loses) in nearly every rollout, so noise picks the move.

Make it default behavior in beryl_search::LongSearch (not a family option, per Derek): a finished game scores for the winner by how soon it ends, discounting each turn past the tree's root, so that a decided position still has a best move: close the game out when ahead, prolong it when behind. Evaluations at cut and eval leaves are discounted alike so the scales agree. Mcts (the Milestone 1 agents) is unchanged.

Measure before and after with the same positions and seeds: how often two searches from different seeds agree on the move, in decided and in contested positions from run-003's logs. Note: every LongSearch family plays differently after this, so run-003 cannot adopt it (its --upgrade check refuses); a new arena run is needed to measure it there.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"a480c222-f15e-4b99-9005-4deeae929976","owner":"derek@fake.email","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:02:24Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-07T06:02:35Z","started_at":"2026-11-07T06:02:35Z","lease_expires_at":"2026-11-07T06:07:35Z","heartbeat_at":"2026-11-07T06:02:35Z"}

