{"id":"by-bajq.6.12","title":"Partner card: Double Major (a copy of a creature spell)","description":"The copies group proved 'a copy of a permanent spell becomes a token as it resolves' (CR 608.3f, CR 707.10) only with a test definition, `Test Twin` ("Copy target creature spell") in `rust/crates/beryl_rules/src/tests/spell_copies.rs` (`a_copy_of_a_creature_spell_becomes_a_token`). No card of the epic copies a creature spell, so no scenario checks that path against XMage and Forge.

Implement Double Major ({G}{U} instant: 'Copy target creature spell you control, except it isn't legendary if the spell is legendary. (A copy of a creature spell becomes a token.)') with `just card new` and the `card-writing` skill. The copy is `Effect::CopySpell` (`beryl_card` effect/mod.rs, builder `copy_spell_except`; Fork in `rust/cards/cards_1993/lea/fork.rs` is the model). 'Isn't legendary' is a new `CopyChange` (a supertype removed), read by layer 1 as `CopyChange::Colors` and `AddSubtype` are (`State::copiable_base`, `Copiable::excepted_subtypes` in `beryl_kernel/src/copiable.rs`); if it can't be said, escalate it in `data/card-escalations.json`, never leave it out.

Scenarios must show: the copy resolves first and is a token creature with the spell's P/T on the battlefield; the original resolves after it as a card; a copy of a legendary creature spell is not legendary, so the legend rule keeps both (use a cheap legendary creature already implemented); the copy is not cast (a 'whenever you cast' trigger sees only the original). Once a scenario covers the token path, delete `Test Twin` and `a_copy_of_a_creature_spell_becomes_a_token` from `spell_copies.rs`.","acceptance_criteria":"Double Major passes `just card check` (Beryl, XMage, Forge) with the scenarios above, and `just specs --shots 'Double Major'` passes. `Test Twin` and its test are deleted. The count gate holds (`just count-gate`).","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-15T11:47:08Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-15T11:52:03Z","started_at":"2026-11-15T11:49:19Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-bajq","enact_actor":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_branch":"enact/by-bajq.6.12","enact_vizier":"d16a0e78-bc6d-4744-8ab1-6e9cdc28b3a2","enact_session":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/by-bajq.6.12","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"9bb447c39489443bbbdbf6ac1077cc4f","enact_pool_session":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:sonnet"]}

{"id":"by-bajq.6.12","title":"Partner card: Double Major (a copy of a creature spell)","description":"The copies group proved 'a copy of a permanent spell becomes a token as it resolves' (CR 608.3f, CR 707.10) only with a test definition, `Test Twin` ("Copy target creature spell") in `rust/crates/beryl_rules/src/tests/spell_copies.rs` (`a_copy_of_a_creature_spell_becomes_a_token`). No card of the epic copies a creature spell, so no scenario checks that path against XMage and Forge.

Implement Double Major ({G}{U} instant: 'Copy target creature spell you control, except it isn't legendary if the spell is legendary. (A copy of a creature spell becomes a token.)') with `just card new` and the `card-writing` skill. The copy is `Effect::CopySpell` (`beryl_card` effect/mod.rs, builder `copy_spell_except`; Fork in `rust/cards/cards_1993/lea/fork.rs` is the model). 'Isn't legendary' is a new `CopyChange` (a supertype removed), read by layer 1 as `CopyChange::Colors` and `AddSubtype` are (`State::copiable_base`, `Copiable::excepted_subtypes` in `beryl_kernel/src/copiable.rs`); if it can't be said, escalate it in `data/card-escalations.json`, never leave it out.

Scenarios must show: the copy resolves first and is a token creature with the spell's P/T on the battlefield; the original resolves after it as a card; a copy of a legendary creature spell is not legendary, so the legend rule keeps both (use a cheap legendary creature already implemented); the copy is not cast (a 'whenever you cast' trigger sees only the original). Once a scenario covers the token path, delete `Test Twin` and `a_copy_of_a_creature_spell_becomes_a_token` from `spell_copies.rs`.","acceptance_criteria":"Double Major passes `just card check` (Beryl, XMage, Forge) with the scenarios above, and `just specs --shots 'Double Major'` passes. `Test Twin` and its test are deleted. The count gate holds (`just count-gate`).","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-15T11:47:08Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-15T11:50:48Z","started_at":"2026-11-15T11:49:19Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-bajq","enact_actor":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_vizier":"d16a0e78-bc6d-4744-8ab1-6e9cdc28b3a2","enact_session":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"9bb447c39489443bbbdbf6ac1077cc4f","enact_pool_session":"local_9e13bde6-7de8-4e57-919b-713047759331","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:sonnet"]}

