acceptance:
Add `just ui-test` checks, using the measuring approach of
`ui/scripts/drive.mjs`'s probes, on a late-game fixture with at least 8
nonland permanents a side and a spell on the stack:
- no P/T badge, loyalty badge or card name is covered;
- sweeping the pointer across each row moves nothing but the hovered card;
- the stack appearing and resolving moves no battlefield card by more than
  4 px;
- the inspector never covers the stack or a life total.

Hovering a card in an overlay opens the inspector (a check).

`just ui-test` checks that:
- one click on a single-use land plays it;
- Escape during target selection cancels, and the card is back in hand;
- after a mouse drag, `getSelection().toString()` is empty;
- Space passes priority;
- a click at the visible strip of each hand card acts on that card;
- menu entries are found by role `button`.

`just ui-test` or fixture checks that:
- an up-to-one-target spell is answered with one targeting step;
- an attack against a player who controls a planeswalker needs no
  attack-target prompt by default;
- explore shows the revealed card;
- a loot's drawn card is visible before the discard is asked.

Rust tests cover any session change.

