body:
Review milestone 6 of epic by-q44s, the Enhanced tier, in rust/beryl3d: beryl_render src/enhanced (mod.rs, shadow.rs, light.rs, bloom.rs and their WGSL files), the Enhanced half of src/renderer.rs and tests/all/shader_cost.rs, beryl_scene src/effects/particles.rs, `Frame::tier`, `Band::Particles` and the tier's use in src/table/shadows.rs, beryl_3d src/tier.rs and the hosts' `tier_can_drop`, the settings row, the gates' Enhanced limits; against docs/beryl-3d.md 'The Enhanced tier', 'Choosing a tier', 'Effects', 'Determinism' and 'Performance gates', and the epic's rules. Fix what you find, with a test for each.

Look hardest at anything that differs between the tiers besides shading:
- a record, a resolved element or a time that is not identical in both tiers, other than contact shadows (Baseline only) and particles (Enhanced only): run the contract's tier check on stress-verbs, stress-hand and stress-stack as well as the gated boards, and at moments with a `vanish`, a lifted card and a shake;
- the client core reading the tier anywhere but `write_shadow` and `effects::particles::write`;
- a step down that changes anything but shading: step down at a moment of each verb in a hand-built script and compare the frames before and after;
- the flat layer: drawn after bloom and the resolve, never multisampled differently from Baseline in a way that moves a glyph's pixels;
- `shake`: added to the same records' screen positions in both tiers, and never to the light-space position the shadow map is drawn and sampled with, so that a shadow moves with its card;
- a card drawn blended in Baseline (dissolve, whiten, opacity under 1) that is drawn opaque, or casts no shadow, in Enhanced in a way that shows;
- particles: a pure function of the run and `now` (draw a moment directly and after stepping every tick), seeded by object id and step, at most 2000, no allocation in `Client::frame`;
- the Baseline shader unchanged (`the_baseline_shader_does_not_change`), the Baseline limits unchanged in data/beryl3d/gates.json, and every gated board still drawn on the downlevel device;
- every pipeline made at startup and every Enhanced target made only when the size changes: no allocation of a GPU object on a frame that starts a script or steps the tier down;
- the probe and the step down: `--probe` and `--tier` exist only in tools builds; a renderer without Enhanced never receives `Tier::Enhanced`; low memory still pins Baseline.

Report in a comment: for each of shadow map, lighting, bloom, multisampling and particles, the recording and moment you looked at with `just b3d png` or `just b3d film --tier enhanced`, and what you changed.

Run: just b3d cargo-test; just b3d test; just b3d gate; just b3d gate --gpu; just b3d lane.


Beads named above: the contract bead (the tier input and the check) is by-q44s.11.2; the renderer skeleton bead is by-q44s.11.3; the shadow map bead by-q44s.11.4; the lighting bead by-q44s.11.5; bloom by-q44s.11.6; particles by-q44s.11.7; the tier choice bead by-q44s.11.8; the settings row by-q44s.11.9; the limits bead by-q44s.11.10; the settings screen bead by-q44s.5.27. Every bead of this milestone depends on by-q44s.4, the review gate before it.

