{"id":"by-q44s.3.44","title":"A resolving spell that exiles itself reaches exile with no step","description":"Symptom: in the recording fork/copies-time-spiral-which-exiles-the-copy-first (both seats, every desktop window), the original Time Spiral (#258) stands on top of the stack while it resolves and then, when script 5 ends, jumps about 1 m to its owner's exile pile with no step. `just b3d test b3d:fork/copies-time-spiral-which-exiles-the-copy-first/you/1600x900` reports it as a rest-placement fault: 'ended the script 999 mm from its resting place'.

Why: while a spell resolves, the game takes it off `view.stack` but its card stays in the stack zone. Beryl 3D now places such a card as the stack's top item (`on_stack` in rust/beryl3d/crates/beryl_scene/src/table/stack.rs); before, it had no place and was simply not drawn. Time Spiral exiles itself as it resolves, but the session's script for that resolution has no step (fly or vanish) for the card's move from the stack to exile, so nothing moves it and the end of the script snaps it to the exile pile.

What to do: find out whether the session's script builder (rust/crates/beryl_protocol/src/script, rust/crates/beryl_session) omits the step for a spell that moves itself to exile as part of its own resolution, and how the web interface shows it (`just b3d timeline`, ui/scripts/timeline.mjs). If the script lacks the step, that is a session change, which reaches both clients (epic rule 7b). If the step is there and Beryl 3D drops it, fix the client. The fault is listed in data/beryl3d/test-faults.json (rest-placement, +1 in each of the 12 tests of the two fork/copies-time-spiral recordings) until this is fixed.","acceptance_criteria":"`just b3d test b3d:fork/copies-time-spiral` passes with the rest-placement entries of those tests lowered by one (`just b3d test --update`), and the original Time Spiral is seen moving from the stack to exile in `just b3d film fork/copies-time-spiral-which-exiles-the-copy-first --from 9700ms --to 10200ms`.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_c30acc3f-956b-47f2-8f8f-3ba99acc7124","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-16T03:13:46Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-16T05:01:10Z","started_at":"2026-11-16T04:59:30Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-q44s","enact_actor":"local_c30acc3f-956b-47f2-8f8f-3ba99acc7124","enact_branch":"enact/by-q44s.3.44","enact_vizier":"32f74257-d3b1-4102-8f70-a1d50feaf650","enact_session":"local_c30acc3f-956b-47f2-8f8f-3ba99acc7124","enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/slot-10","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"f47981b14a22410294e4351b29c4b061","enact_pool_session":"local_c30acc3f-956b-47f2-8f8f-3ba99acc7124","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:opus"]}

