Proposed design: compile a script resumably. Laying the script out in time (`beat::lay_out` over its `StepTiming`s) is cheap and stays whole, so every step's start and end are known at once. The per-step part (`Motion::step`, the effects and the sounds of each step) runs in order, up to a fixed number of steps per frame, and must reach each step before the frame in which that step begins. A beat's steps start together, so the frame that receives the script compiles at least its first beat; later beats start at least one beat's duration later (hundreds of milliseconds, so tens of frames), which leaves room to spread them. Sketch:

