{"id":"by-q44s.7.18","title":"Run interface checks at the three phone sizes","description":"Read docs/beryl-3d.md “Interface checks” and “Test speed”. beryl_scene src/agent/checks.rs already has on_screen, reachable and phone_sizes, with 44 and 11 in data/beryl3d/gates.json. Reuse them. The gaps are the default Insets in beryl_scene src/driver/mod.rs Page::begin and Page::context, and a desktop-only matrix in beryl_inspect src/pages.rs (DESKTOP_WINDOWS, page, check_recording), src/runner.rs (tests, Test::page), src/cli/test.rs (test, context) and src/cli/options.rs (Options::test_name). Add the three phone sizes (393×759, 375×647, 430×932) per recorded seat. Use deterministic synthetic insets in the phone fixture path: top 44, bottom 34, sides 0, with asymmetric side insets exercised in the scene tests. Feed the same insets to Input::Surface and Context; mark them as test geometry, independent of the native host. Reproduction by b3d:<recording>/<seat>/<size> in tree/check must select the same layout and insets; normal flags keep their advertised default size. Leave the existing test names intact.

Register --phone-only for just b3d test in beryl_inspect src/cli/mod.rs and route the matrix selection through the existing tools/src/beryl_tools/beryl3d lane and sweep invocation path. Keep the regular lane and sweep desktop-only during build-out. The layout Warden enables the combined matrix after the full portrait run passes. Phone-only runs work with --every-tick and report all rules; do not add allowances for unfinished portrait UI or change the existing test-fault counts. Be sure --phone-only cannot age out or update desktop allowances. Reuse the existing check times via Page::check_all. Read ui/scripts/phone-faults.mjs phoneFaults for clipping and scroll intent; Beryl 3D's own 44/11 values still apply.

Tests in beryl_inspect tests/all/runner.rs: enumerate seven sizes including both recorded seats; agree on phone layout/insets between test, tree and check; preserve desktop reproduction and isolate phone-only selection. beryl_scene tests/all/agent.rs and widgets.rs: enabled flat target with each edge spilling into an inset faults, a fully safe 44-point target and 11-point line pass, and one logical point under either size fails. Run: just b3d cargo-test -p beryl_scene --test all agent::; just b3d cargo-test -p beryl_scene --test all widgets::; just b3d cargo-test -p beryl_inspect --test all runner::; just b3d test --help. Run the phone-only pay-default prefix and verify it evaluates all three portrait sizes and names the reproductions, while reporting any preexisting UI faults for the downstream beads.","acceptance_criteria":"The tests prove the phone window cases reach the existing checks with nonzero insets, fault reproductions replay the same window, and the desktop gate still passes.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_c8346685-d6fa-402c-b1e7-d2c34a1887ca","owner":"derek@fake.email","created_at":"2026-11-16T15:19:00Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-16T21:33:16Z","started_at":"2026-11-16T21:25:52Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-q44s","enact_actor":"local_c8346685-d6fa-402c-b1e7-d2c34a1887ca","enact_branch":"enact/by-q44s.7.18","enact_vizier":"32f74257-d3b1-4102-8f70-a1d50feaf650","enact_session":"local_c8346685-d6fa-402c-b1e7-d2c34a1887ca","enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/slot-10","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"1ed5b4d65f90452bb0938cee740b7a02","enact_pool_session":"local_c8346685-d6fa-402c-b1e7-d2c34a1887ca","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:opus"]}

