{"id":"by-q44s.7.20","title":"Lay out game furniture and prompts on phones","description":"Read docs/beryl-3d.md “The flat layer”, “Sizes” and “Interface checks”. In beryl_scene src/screens/game.rs add game_phone and route it from screens/mod.rs screen using the shared selector. Keep ScreenIn, Element, widgets and Press decisions from desktop. In src/client/screen.rs Client::show_screen/show_gear and src/client/mod.rs Client::resize, rebuild at input time when geometry changes and keep furniture present at idle priority and between prompts. Prefer the desktop screen's prepared view data from ScreenIn over recomputing shapes in Client::frame. src/hud/players.rs players, hud/steps.rs steps and hud/log.rs log are the existing pieces; use the completed milestone 3 versions. Add portrait compositions of existing prompt widgets in src/prompts/mod.rs screen and src/prompts/bar.rs prompt_bar. Use the table bead's bands and occupancy for the prompt pill, giving it the nearest clear position to the middle line, with that line as the fallback. Put primary actions in the bottom dock, phase and the turn banner in the middle, undo/full control across from phase, and life/mana by each side. Follow docs/ui-conventions.md “The phone” for the step banner, scry pill, combined graveyard/exile sheet and revealed-card pile. Keep settings, log and bug report reachable from the menu. Respect native safe area and keep text at least 11 points and controls at least 44 square. Reuse existing viewer, settings, choice and tray elements and messages. Leave opening/game result composition and non-game sheets to the other screen bead; keep those dispatch branches additive so the two beads can land independently.

Web references: stage/PhoneStageBoard.tsx PhoneStageBoard puts the orbs, piles, trays, phase strip, dock and menu in the bands. stage/PhoneChrome.tsx PileButtons, Menu, LogSheet, ManaSheet, PileSheet, Inspected and Notices give the sheet behavior; mobile/chrome.tsx Orb, Middle and useViewport give strip positions and the bottom-panel reservation. mobile/faces.tsx CardScan and PileTop describe card displays; use the native card renderer. stage/PromptBar.tsx PhonePromptDock and PhonePromptOver use mobile/asked.ts askedTop, including the tapped footprint and fallback. ui/src/mobile/phone.css supplies the relative layout of strips, sheets and dock.

Tests in beryl_scene tests/all/game_phone.rs: idle game furniture exists without an open prompt; a stack or board target occupies the middle without obscuring prompt targets; prompt actions send the existing decisions; open and dismiss a pile and log sheet; safe interactive extents at all three sizes including on resize. Run: just b3d cargo-test -p beryl_scene --test all game_phone; just b3d test b3d:pay-default --phone-only; just b3d tree b3d:pay-default/you/375x647 --at end. Use the stock recordings on both seats wherever offered.","acceptance_criteria":"Game furniture, prompts and in-game sheets are reachable and pass the interface rules at all three sizes for both recorded seats. Existing prompt actions and the desktop game tests pass.","status":"in_progress","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_c8470108-bf28-4da5-bc23-92fa9750dc77","owner":"derek@fake.email","created_at":"2026-11-16T15:19:07Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-16T23:23:55Z","started_at":"2026-11-16T22:34:13Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-q44s","enact_actor":"local_c8470108-bf28-4da5-bc23-92fa9750dc77","enact_branch":"enact/by-q44s.7.20","enact_vizier":"32f74257-d3b1-4102-8f70-a1d50feaf650","enact_session":"local_c8470108-bf28-4da5-bc23-92fa9750dc77","enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/slot-10","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"f457079e121a4147ad235f092c807bc1","enact_pool_session":"local_c8470108-bf28-4da5-bc23-92fa9750dc77","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:opus"]}

