{"id":"by-q44s.7.20","title":"Lay out game furniture and prompts on phones","description":"Read docs/beryl-3d.md “The flat layer”, “Sizes” and “Interface checks”. In beryl_scene src/screens/game.rs add game_phone and route it from screens/mod.rs screen using the shared selector. Keep ScreenIn, Element, widgets and Press decisions from desktop. In src/client/screen.rs Client::show_screen/show_gear and src/client/mod.rs Client::resize, rebuild at input time when geometry changes and keep furniture present at idle priority and between prompts. Prefer the desktop screen's prepared view data from ScreenIn over recomputing shapes in Client::frame. src/hud/players.rs players, hud/steps.rs steps and hud/log.rs log are the existing pieces; use the completed milestone 3 versions. Add portrait compositions of existing prompt widgets in src/prompts/mod.rs screen and src/prompts/bar.rs prompt_bar. Use the table bead's bands and occupancy for the prompt pill, giving it the nearest clear position to the middle line, with that line as the fallback. Put primary actions in the bottom dock, phase and the turn banner in the middle, undo/full control across from phase, and life/mana by each side. Follow docs/ui-conventions.md “The phone” for the step banner, scry pill, combined graveyard/exile sheet and revealed-card pile. Keep settings, log and bug report reachable from the menu. Respect native safe area and keep text at least 11 points and controls at least 44 square. Reuse existing viewer, settings, choice and tray elements and messages. Leave opening/game result composition and non-game sheets to the other screen bead; keep those dispatch branches additive so the two beads can land independently.

