{"id":"by-q44s.7.21","title":"Lay out start, overlays and other screens on phones","description":"Read docs/beryl-3d.md “The flat layer” and “Sizes”. In beryl_scene src/screens keep the existing screen/widget/state APIs. Add portrait functions in start.rs (start_phone), opening.rs (opening_phone), game_over.rs (game_over_phone and its action dock), settings.rs, bug_report.rs, gallery.rs, testing.rs and table.rs for the entries these use. Select each alternate through the shared Layout::for_size selector in its existing public function so the game-furniture bead can edit game.rs and client routing independently. Reuse Element, Press, FieldState, the native client field requests and the desktop screen functions' form/action builders. Give long content a bounded scroll area, keep primary actions inside the usable bottom edge, and ensure every exposed action remains reachable when a field is in focus. Reflow current desktop gallery, testing and table entry widgets as a single safe-area column. On start, preserve agent selection, seed, fair setting and pending/error states; use a one-column agent list with scroll when needed. On opening keep and mulligan, keep the card selection above the dock; present the game's result and buttons in portrait. The bug report uses the existing desktop draft and submit actions in a bottom sheet over the frozen view. No host or keyboard implementation is in this bead.

