{"id":"by-q44s.81","title":"Beryl 3D tool changes run the whole python test suite","description":"Symptom: a push that changed only Beryl 3D's code and its tools (tools/src/beryl_tools/beryl3d/) ran the main python lane: black, pyre and all of pytest, including tests such as test_bisect.py (33 s) and test_checks.py (28 s) that have nothing to do with Beryl 3D. In milestone 2 that cost 1,628 s of lane time over 6 pushes. docs/checks.md 'Beryl 3D' says this is by design, but it goes against C17's aim that Beryl 3D's changes run only Beryl 3D's checks.

