body:
Review by-q44s.9.21, which finishes the parity list's fixtures, card specs, verbs, effects, marks and prompt shapes once the M4 phone beads (by-q44s.7.26 to 7.33) have landed. Read docs/beryl-3d.md "The parity list", "Sizes" and "Interface checks" and rust/beryl3d/AGENTS.md, then the bead's diff (beryl_scene src/table/phone.rs, src/table/rows.rs, src/prompts, src/verbs and tests/all, as touched).

Look hardest at:
- a fix that passes a phone rule by changing the rule or its gates (beryl_scene src/agent/checks.rs, src/agent/steps.rs, data/beryl3d/gates.json audit.phone_target_points) instead of the placement, or any phone allowance in data/beryl3d/test-faults.json;
- desktop timelines or desktop layout changed by a phone fix;
- new allocations or layout work in `Client::frame`;
- tests that assert positions instead of the rule that failed.

If by-q44s.9.21 closed with no change, confirm its parity comment and that `just b3d parity --full` still shows those lines complete.

