{"id":"by-q44s.9.33","title":"Beryl 3D bug reports record the build commit","description":"Symptom: a bug report saved from Beryl 3D (Cmd+B in the beryl3d app) carries commit: unknown in its fields, so `just b3d bug <report>` prints 'built from unknown' and a worker cannot tell which commit the report came from.

Why: the web app's shell calls `beryl_session::bugs::set_build_commit(env!("BERYL_COMMIT"))` (rust/crates/beryl_app/src/lib.rs:273), with BERYL_COMMIT set by rust/crates/beryl_app/build.rs. The beryl3d binary (rust/beryl3d/crates/beryl_3d, which has its own build.rs) never calls it.

Do: set BERYL_COMMIT in rust/beryl3d/crates/beryl_3d/build.rs as beryl_app's build.rs does, and call set_build_commit at the app's start (src/app.rs or main). Weigh the cost: beryl_app's rerun-if-changed on HEAD relinks the crate on every commit; keep the env var confined to the binary crate so the scene and inspect crates do not rebuild. Extend rust/beryl3d/crates/beryl_3d/tests/all/bugs.rs to check the report's commit is not 'unknown'. Run just b3d cargo-test and just test-py tests/test_beryl3d_bug.py.","status":"in_progress","priority":3,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_a7495650-d08e-4f4d-b32a-0e4e9169d07b","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-17T01:57:07Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-17T05:47:23Z","started_at":"2026-11-17T05:45:43Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-q44s","enact_actor":"local_a7495650-d08e-4f4d-b32a-0e4e9169d07b","enact_branch":"enact/by-q44s.9.33","enact_vizier":"32f74257-d3b1-4102-8f70-a1d50feaf650","enact_session":"local_a7495650-d08e-4f4d-b32a-0e4e9169d07b","enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/slot-01","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"66f2e01f95944f4492fa326c6fa0c8bc","enact_pool_session":"local_a7495650-d08e-4f4d-b32a-0e4e9169d07b","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["role:executor","tier:sonnet"]}

