Ideas to measure, cheapest first: (1) what the registry's 1.0 s is (its 50,000-entry CARDS gathering by const evaluation in beryl_cards/src/lib.rs, `gathered`; its names module, measured as negligible) and whether CARDS can be gathered at first use like scenarios(); (2) whether the set crate's build script can skip rewriting cards.rs when its text is unchanged, and whether `rerun-if-changed` on each set directory instead of the crate root cuts cargo's stat work; (3) why an incremental recheck of a 1,350-card crate after one new item costs 1.2 s (rustc -Z self-profile on nightly); (4) smaller set crates only if data/set-groups.json's rule changes, which is the plan's decision K8. Land speedups in the real tree, re-run `just scale --assert`, and when the measure meets 2 s, drop the held limit in scale.py's BUDGETS (it holds the measure at 4.1 s meanwhile) and update docs/project-50k.md's Measurements.","acceptance_criteria":"`just scale --assert` at 50,000 cards meets the plan's 2 s one-edit rebuild budget with the held limit removed from BUDGETS in scale.py, or the bead records each attempt's numbers and cause; the other three budgets still pass; `just check` passes.","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_5eb7b5f3-15d8-4222-8a55-d90df9b406fc","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-13T01:46:53Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-13T01:52:38Z","started_at":"2026-11-13T01:48:19Z","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-w8gv","enact_actor":"local_5eb7b5f3-15d8-4222-8a55-d90df9b406fc","enact_branch":"enact/by-w8gv.13.14","enact_vizier":"232e381d-446b-48dc-b742-bf52bcb7ad09","enact_session":"local_5eb7b5f3-15d8-4222-8a55-d90df9b406fc","enact_recovery":"[{"owner": "vizier:jarvis:claude:232e381d-446b-48dc-b742-bf52bcb7ad09", "session": null, "vizier": "232e381d-446b-48dc-b742-bf52bcb7ad09", "provider": "claude", "app": "claude", "project": "/Users/dthurn/beryl", "spawn_host": "jarvis", "host": null, "path": null, "branch": null,