{"id":"by-w8gv.21.16","title":"Board chrome and pointer input around the stage","description":"Everything on the game screen that is neither motion nor a prompt, rebuilt around the stage in files under 800 lines, and the one way the stage reports the pointer. Board.tsx is deleted at the cut-over (by-w8gv.21.32), never split in place (epic by-w8gv.21, Milestone 6).

Read first: the epic by-w8gv.21 (the user's decisions, what was agreed with the CI track, the code map); docs/project-50k.md, Target architecture, Presentation (K22 to K31); docs/ui-conventions.md (generated from data/ui-conventions.json: edit the data). Then the stage lane's handoffs (by-w8gv.21.13, by-w8gv.21.14, by-w8gv.21.15).

## Chrome

ui/src/game/Board.tsx is one component (Board, about lines 257 to 2057) and its helpers. Under ?stage, desktop and phone, the stage board shows:

- life orbs and incoming damage (Life, Incoming: about 2242 to 2337);
- the step banner (StepBanner, useBannerUp: 2079 to 2138), TurnBanner.tsx and Narration.tsx;
- concede, undo, settings and full control (ConcedeButton, UndoButton, Gear, FullControlIcon);
- the stack peek (StackPeek, 2540);
- pile buttons and the zone viewer (ui/src/game/Piles.tsx), mana pools (ui/src/components/Mana.tsx), the log (ui/src/game/log.ts) and the bug-report button;
- hover inspection (Piles.tsx useHoverInspect, Inspect, inspectorBox; Board's InspectAt at 3299 and inspectorPlace at 2155; settled entry: Hover inspection).

Reuse components that are already files of their own. Where code must come out of Board.tsx, move it to a shared file that both boards import: the old board keeps working until the cut-over, and behavior is never forked. If by-w8gv.21.8 made step and turn announcements verbs, their banners follow the stage's current step, not a timer.

## Pointer input

One small typed interface from the stage to React: hover (enter and leave, with the object), click, and a card dragged onto an object or a player. Today that is CardLayer.tsx's under() (about line 975) with its Drop and Onto types (64 to 75) and physics.ts useCardPhysics for the held card. Hover inspection uses it here; the shape beads (by-w8gv.21.26 on) use click and drag. A held card is the one pose the pointer drives and not the clock: say how it enters the model (pose() must still return it) and keep it testable.

## Checks

Generic audits, not scripted checks (AGENTS.md, Checks; plan K20): shots under ?stage for the fixtures that show each piece (ui/shots.json), passing screenFaults and crowdedControls. Only if no audit can express a property, one check in ui/scripts/verbs.mjs with a comment saying why.

## Not to read

The Prompt, Declare, Finish, TriggerOrder and ActionMenu parts of Board.tsx (from about line 2777): those are the shape beads'. beats.ts.

## Parity and policy

Parity at the push (plan K11): just check passes; the frozen save corpus replays (cargo test -p beryl_session --test corpus); rollouts_never_change holds (rust/crates/beryl_bench/src/rollout.rs); slow CI's counts lane passes with no bump (405,276,238). Nothing waits on the user (K31): where his eye is wanted, proceed on Arena or the nearest existing verb and file a bead labelled human that nothing depends on. Record decisions and deviations as comments on this bead. A bar missed after three attempts is recorded on the epic with its measured value and cause, a follow-up is filed and the work goes on.
