body:
**Reworked 2026-11-11 (the user): motion is Beryl's own, judged independently; see by-w8gv.21.42 and the epic's comment.**

Every way a card or permanent changes zone on the stage, beyond the first slice's cast, landing and token.

Read first: the epic by-w8gv.21 (the user's decisions, what was agreed with the CI track, the code map); docs/project-50k.md, Target architecture, Presentation (K22 to K31); docs/ui-conventions.md (generated from data/ui-conventions.json: edit the data). Then the stage lane's handoffs (by-w8gv.21.13, by-w8gv.21.14, by-w8gv.21.15), by-w8gv.21.8's table of verbs and by-w8gv.21.19's handoff.

## Cases

Take the list from by-w8gv.21.8's table; these are the ones known today, with the convention entry that rules each:

- draws, yours and the opponent's; deals and staggered draws (opening hands);
- discard; mill and other moves from a library, hand or graveyard shown face up in a row before they land (ui/src/game/layout.ts SHOWCASE and showcasePlace, about 425 to 460), from both seats;
- a permanent that leaves dissolves in place (Permanents that leave; ui/src/game/dissolve.ts); a token that leaves (not-seen);
- a spell resolving to the graveyard, or to the top or bottom of a library (ZoneChange.library_top);
- a countered spell (A countered spell: it leaves first; the strike on it is by-w8gv.21.21's verb, composed here);
- returns to hand (An opponent's spell returned to hand; not-seen: Your own spell returned to hand);
- exile: A batch exile; linked exile under its host (exception 6) and its return (not-seen; linkedReturnFlights in beats.ts);
- a card cast from a graveyard or from exile;
- the shuffle; the opponent's scry; the flights after the local player's scry is answered (The local player's scry; A card a look puts in the graveyard; not-seen: Cards a look returns). The scry flight is one of the five repeated themes, 7 reports: its motion is this bead's named case, citing the report beads (bd list --label bug-report --all --limit 0), and its prompt is by-w8gv.21.27's;
- the opponent's cards lifting while they look at them (Cards the opponent looks at; PlayerView.handling; liftsHandling in layout.ts);
- a creature that enters attacking, a card that enters or turns face down (not-seen).

## For each verb case

- The stage's track in ui/src/stage (as by-w8gv.21.14 laid the slice's verbs out), with its values in data/ui-conventions.json: Beryl's own, designed for Beryl's cards, starting from Arena's clip, numbers and prose description in data/arena-motion.json (by-w8gv.21.18) but never copying them (by-w8gv.21.42).
- A hand-written script snapshot in Rust (by-w8gv.21.9 and by-w8gv.21.10 wrote one per verb; add a case that is missing).
- Checks verb:<name>/<seat>/<layout> for both seats and both layouts in ui/scripts/verbs.mjs: one check per verb with its cases inside, never one per card. Positions come from spec moments (just specs --describe <card>) or scripted boards (rust/crates/beryl_cli/src/boards.rs, recorded into ui/fixtures.json). Stage time only.
- by-w8gv.21.19's checks hold the values to Arena. A verb that is a numbered Beryl exception is marked exempt in the data. A case the recordings do not show is composed from existing verbs and listed under not-seen (K29).
- Today's code is the list of cases, not the design: it is deleted at the cut-over.

Today's code for these: ui/src/game/CardLayer.tsx useGlide (about lines 365 to 956), choiceFlight.ts, flight.ts.

## Parity and policy

Parity at the push (plan K11): just check passes; the frozen save corpus replays (cargo test -p beryl_session --test corpus); rollouts_never_change holds (rust/crates/beryl_bench/src/rollout.rs); slow CI's counts lane passes with no bump (405,276,238). Nothing waits on the user (K31): where his eye is wanted, proceed on Arena or the nearest existing verb and file a bead labelled human that nothing depends on. Record decisions and deviations as comments on this bead. A bar missed after three attempts is recorded on the epic with its measured value and cause, a follow-up is filed and the work goes on.

