- A hand-written script snapshot in Rust (by-w8gv.21.9 and by-w8gv.21.10 wrote one per verb; add a case that is missing).
- Checks verb:<name>/<seat>/<layout> for both seats and both layouts in ui/scripts/verbs.mjs: one check per verb with its cases inside, never one per card. Positions come from spec moments (just specs --describe <card>) or scripted boards (rust/crates/beryl_cli/src/boards.rs, recorded into ui/fixtures.json). Stage time only.
- by-w8gv.21.19's checks hold the values to Arena. A verb that is a numbered Beryl exception is marked exempt in the data. A case the recordings do not show is composed from existing verbs and listed under not-seen (K29).
- Today's code is the list of cases, not the design: it is deleted at the cut-over.

