**Reworked 2026-11-11 (the user): motion is Beryl's own, judged independently; see by-w8gv.21.42 and the epic's comment.**

Every visible change that leaves a card where it is, and every change to a player, on the stage.

Read first: the epic by-w8gv.21 (the user's decisions, what was agreed with the CI track, the code map); docs/project-50k.md, Target architecture, Presentation (K22 to K31); docs/ui-conventions.md (generated from data/ui-conventions.json: edit the data). Then the stage lane's handoffs, by-w8gv.21.8's table of verbs and by-w8gv.21.20's handoff if it has closed.

## Cases

Take the list from by-w8gv.21.8's table; known today:

- tap and untap (exception 2: full cards that tap). Today a fixed wait orders a tap before a departure (beats.ts HOLD.tapBeforeMove); on the stage the script orders them;
- a card turning face up or over (not-seen: A card turning face up);
- counters added and removed, loyalty, power and toughness changing;
- life gained and lost on the orbs, and incoming damage (Board.tsx Life and Incoming, about 2242 to 2337);
- damage: the strike on a creature, a player or a planeswalker; combat damage dealt both ways at once; the strike on a countered spell (CardLayer's shake);
- attaching and unattaching (attachments() in layout.ts, about 1375; BENEATH_STEP);
- control changing: the card crosses the table;
- the coin flip (coinFlipBanner, Board.tsx about 2762);
- neighbors making room: how the cards at rest move when one arrives or leaves, including lands piling (exception 5: unstacked until seven). One rule for every row, on both layouts.

## For each verb case

- The stage's track in ui/src/stage (as by-w8gv.21.14 laid the slice's verbs out), with its values in data/ui-conventions.json: Beryl's own, designed for Beryl's cards, starting from Arena's clip, numbers and prose description in data/arena-motion.json (by-w8gv.21.18) but never copying them (by-w8gv.21.42).
- A hand-written script snapshot in Rust (by-w8gv.21.9 and by-w8gv.21.10 wrote one per verb; add a case that is missing).
- Checks verb:<name>/<seat>/<layout> for both seats and both layouts in ui/scripts/verbs.mjs: one check per verb with its cases inside, never one per card. Positions come from spec moments (just specs --describe <card>) or scripted boards (rust/crates/beryl_cli/src/boards.rs, recorded into ui/fixtures.json). Stage time only.
- by-w8gv.21.19's checks hold the values to Arena. A verb that is a numbered Beryl exception is marked exempt in the data. A case the recordings do not show is composed from existing verbs and listed under not-seen (K29).
- Today's code is the list of cases, not the design: it is deleted at the cut-over.

## Parity and policy

Parity at the push (plan K11): just check passes; the frozen save corpus replays (cargo test -p beryl_session --test corpus); rollouts_never_change holds (rust/crates/beryl_bench/src/rollout.rs); slow CI's counts lane passes with no bump (405,276,238). Nothing waits on the user (K31): where his eye is wanted, proceed on Arena or the nearest existing verb and file a bead labelled human that nothing depends on. Record decisions and deviations as comments on this bead. A bar missed after three attempts is recorded on the epic with its measured value and cause, a follow-up is filed and the work goes on.

