{"id":"by-xe6n","title":"Delete flaky check rust:beryl_session::clicks::a_session_takes_clicks_and_its_latest_view_keeps_the_prompt","description":"The check `rust:beryl_session::clicks::a_session_takes_clicks_and_its_latest_view_keeps_the_prompt` (lane `rust`) failed and then passed on its rerun on the same tree in `by ci` on JARVIS at 1197fe04c5. The flake failed no lane, but checks must fail deterministically, so the flaky one is deleted instead of being rerun until it passes. `just ci-report` lists its runs, failures and verdicts; its bead of verdicts is by-ci-15e41eed18.

Before deleting it, ask: could a fast, deterministic test (a Rust unit test, a Node test with no browser, a check against a recorded fixture) keep most of what this check protects? If so, write that test, then delete this check. If not, delete it when it has never caught a real bug (no `catch` verdict), or move it to the nightly when it has. If the flake comes from a race in the product rather than in the test, fix the race instead and say so.

Record on this bead which you chose and why.","acceptance_criteria":"`rust:beryl_session::clicks::a_session_takes_clicks_and_its_latest_view_keeps_the_prompt` no longer runs in CI, or it is replaced by a deterministic test, and this bead records which and why.","status":"open","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","owner":"ci@example.com","created_at":"2026-11-13T18:10:27Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-13T18:10:27Z","metadata":{"beryl_flaky_check":"rust:beryl_session::clicks::a_session_takes_clicks_and_its_latest_view_keeps_the_prompt"},"labels":["flaky-check","tier:opus"]}

