{"notes":"Reproduced the report in the live Playground moment adeline-resplendent-cathar/playground-adelines-human-attacks-a-planeswalker-0/yours and in a headless regression (failed on animation frame 0 before the fix). Report has fixture, view, UI log and journal; no screenshot or replay. The recorded pending slots change from Adeline (1) to Human (120) while Adeline's committed target is Teferi (65). d206c617 is an ancestor of reported e7274440 and follows moving arrow endpoints. Here the transient trigger beat instead lacked the declared combat data, so the line had no owner during playback.

The fix replays the attack declaration in the shared beat builder before cutting the trigger beat and tracks each pending attacker as it enters/leaves or declares. The line renderer, chevron tracking and unrelated arrows use the same board data as before. Verified live yours (219 frames): Adeline stayed linked to Teferi across trigger, Human entrance and chooser; Human gained its own line to the opponent upon selection. Theirs (325 frames): the scripted Adeline remained linked to the defending player, the pending Human gained a separate line to Teferi once chosen, and both cleared after combat. The sampled paths tracked their chevron tips within 1 pixel. Neighbor tests passed for draft retargeting, transition to blockers, and departing planeswalkers from both seats. The focused regression is run with just ui-test "declared attack lines survive". Both-seat driver snippets, frame summaries and screenshots are in /Users/dthurn/Library/Caches/beryl/spec-drive/attack-line-lifetime/20261110-081601-98373. CI disposition will follow.
Parent observed CI at 80863250 fail the new declared attack lines survive a token defender choice test: the Human’s chooser opened assertion at interactions.mjs:10800. See .git/enact/ci-check.log. Prior 4990cfb1 failure was a different stack target arrow test; its focused rerun passed. Please diagnose/repair the combat test once the Steward claim is available, or coordinate via bead."}

