{"id":"by-zf0.9","title":"Paused resolution re-runs answer by index across slot rebindings","description":"Found in by-zf0.7 (commit 2ecf20af). A live game panicked in freeze-saves: `just freeze-saves --games 184 --seed 522000000` (game i=183, seed 522000183; use `cargo run --release -p beryl_cli -- freeze-saves <empty dir> --games 184 --seed 522000000`). Panic: beryl_engine effect.rs ask_object 'an answer among the objects', from Thirst for Discovery (beryl_cards blue/thirst_for_discovery.rs draw_three_discard) resolving for the agent (P1), turn 26.

What happens: a paused resolution keeps its answers as candidate indices (Resolving.record, resolve.rs run/resolve/replay_to_question, effect.rs EffectCtx::ask). The agent was handed the second discard with 8 candidates (session game.rs next_view, At::Agent from engine next -> r.question) and answered 7; the re-run that applies record [1, 5, 7] asks that discard with 7 candidates. The hand strings match between runs, so index 5 of the first discard named a different Plains in different runs (the hand holds 2 Plains both players know and 1 only its owner knows; engine::collapse keeps those apart since by-zf0.8). Likely cause: runs of one paused body bind cards to slots differently (the resolve run lends chance via the sink, view/replay runs do not; keep_what_was_seen in resolve.rs copies identities only when settled && !random), so a recorded index means a different card. Reverting by-zf0.7's batch order (event.rs in_order) hides it for this seed because the draw order changes, but staging's design has the same fragility.

Fix direction: make a paused body's runs agree on slot identities, or record paused answers by what they do (as save::Chosen does) rather than by index.","acceptance_criteria":"The repro above plays without panic; a test pauses a body over a hand with copies known to different players and resumes it with the same answer meaning the same card; docs/bugs.md entry.","status":"closed","priority":1,"issue_type":"task","assignee":"local_b5d21bc7-c111-4eaa-95e0-15cd24184dd8","owner":"derek@fake.email","created_at":"2026-11-08T19:46:53Z","created_by":"Derek Thurn","updated_at":"2026-11-08T20:12:43Z","started_at":"2026-11-08T19:48:14Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T20:11:13Z","close_reason":"Paused bodies rerun from their first knowledge; repro plays through (cb392028)","metadata":{"enact_run":"by-zf0","enact_runs":"by-zf0","enact_actor":"local_b5d21bc7-c111-4eaa-95e0-15cd24184dd8","enact_branch":"enact/by-zf0.9","enact_vizier":"b75bcd53-3779-4162-86d9-e3261503c5a7","enact_commits":"cb3920285d8d1e1f8cb32da061d3fb93765874dc","enact_session":"local_b5d21bc7-c111-4eaa-95e0-15cd24184dd8","enact_archived":false,"enact_worktree":"/Users/dthurn/beryl/.worktrees/by-zf0.9","enact_spawn_app":"claude","enact_spawn_host":"jarvis","enact_reservation":"cb681be5796d45faa1fe4f731dd9a25b","enact_spawn_project":"/Users/dthurn/beryl","enact_worktree_host":"jarvis","enact_spawn_provider":"claude"},"labels":["lane:saves","role:executor"]}

